# Cursor IDE Rules — Orthogonal Engineering
# These rules apply to all Cursor AI sessions in this repository.

## Identity

You are a software engineering agent with full write access.
You are NOT a warden. You are NOT read-only.

## Required Reading

Before any code change, read:
1. SOP_AI_HANDSHAKE.md
2. .github/copilot-instructions.md
3. STANDARDS_REGISTRY.json (query with: python tools/standards_check.py --list)

## Mandatory Consent Step

Before changing code, run:
  python tools/append_consent.py --candidate-id "cursor-<date>" --authoriser "@aidoruao" --action "<slug>" --scope-glob "<glob>" --justification "<reason>"

## Code Rules

- NO float() — use Fraction from fractions module
- All check functions return Tuple[bool, ProofObject]
- All docstrings include "Falsifies if:" AND "falsifies_if:" (both forms)
- No assert — use ProofObject for failures
- No stubs (no pass, no NotImplementedError)
- mypy --strict compatible type annotations
- Tests runnable with pytest

## Domain Pattern

```python
from fractions import Fraction
from typing import Tuple
from axioms.logic import ProofObject

def check_something() -> Tuple[bool, ProofObject]:
    """
    Invariant: description.
    Standard: ref
    Falsifies if: condition
    falsifies_if: condition
    """
    val = Fraction(1, 3)
    ok = val > Fraction(0)
    proof = ProofObject(rule="Rule", premises=[f"val={val}"], conclusion="OK" if ok else "FAIL")
    return ok, proof
```

## File Structure

- src/sal/ — SAL kernel (adjoint triple, topos, forcing, realizability)
- kernel/ — capability-gated kernel modules
- src/domains/ — 163 domain invariant packages
- tests/ — pytest test files
- tools/ — utility scripts

## Behavioral Constraints

- Append-only: never delete AGENT_FEED.md rows or consent log entries
- No Recursive Wipe (rm -rf, shutil.rmtree, etc.)
- No defamation — capability comparison only
- Consent before kernel surface changes

## Verify Changes

  python tools/state_witness/generate_feed_entry.py --verify
  python audit/popperian_audit.py 2>&1 | tail -3
  python tools/standards_check.py --verify
  pytest tests/ -q
